A||||2||Uaana||Armrest seperation||||1||
Z||000000||Uaana||09-06-2000||09:48 PM||||Just recently my arm rest has been seperating from the door. I pull the door shut and the upper part of the handle seperates from the door. <BR>Now Ive pulled the screw and reseated the plug and then put the screw back in. still dont work right.<BR>Any suggestions?||||reg||1
Z||000001||HugGRRRFiero||09-06-2000||10:13 PM||||Check to make sure the bottom two screws that run upward on the underside of the armrest are tight also.<P>If that doesn't work, then you probably will need to pull the door panel off to get a look at the brackets that the armrest screws go into.  The rivets that hold those brackets on might be loose.  If the rivets are bad and you don't have a Big Daddy rivet gun to replace them, then you probably could drill out the rivets and replace them with some short bolts, lock nuts and washers.  Make sure tho that the door window will have clearance to the bolts when you raise and lower it.<P>Brent<P>------------------<BR>    <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/huggrrr.gif">  <BR>  <A HREF="mailto:HugGRRRFiero@hotmail.com">HugGRRRFiero@hotmail.com</A> ||||reg||3
Z||000002||theogre||09-07-2000||12:10 AM||||IF you are describing what it sounds like..... you need a new arm rest. The hard plastic inside the rest has broken at the top. It's a common problem with this style rest.<P>The bracket it screws into it heavily rivited to the door. If the screw is tight and not stripped I'd suspect the armrest more than the bracket.||||reg||1
